`EventTicket` gains indexes on `created` and `closed_at`. Neither was indexed, and both carry the range scans the ticket-flow queries make. This is the whole of the schema Phase 5B adds - the phase introduces no model and no counter.

The app now ships one page template, and [ADR 0008](../docs/decisions/0008-ui-component-framework-only.md) carries an amendment saying why. Nautobot's UI Component Framework renders panels inside an object detail page, and core ships no template that takes a bare list of panels, so a dashboard with no object behind it needs a file of its own. It extends `base.html` alone and draws no layout of its own: the panel grid is core's `components/layout/two_over_one.html`, included rather than copied, so this page moves when every other page does. `TemplateGuardTest` changes from a flat prohibition to a one-file allowlist, and additionally asserts that the allowed file extends nothing but the base and emits no grid or table markup the framework owns - which is the coupling the ADR was actually about, and is not the same claim as "it has one file".
